    [CI][Test] Add singlecard operator tests to nightly (#18431)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    - Enable `singlecard_ops/` nightly on A3-560T and A5 with 8-card
    runners; keep 310P scheduling unchanged.
    - Align operator test entries, device guards/API calls and shared
    test-state cleanup.
    - Replace large parameter grids with reviewed scenarios while preserving
    targeted regressions.
    - Keep known hardware/compiler/operator issues as precise skips;
    operator implementations are unchanged.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    No production behavior changes.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - Observed recursive suite: 112 test files and 2,619 collected cases.
    The scenario reduction and upstream cases are retained.
    - A2 / 910B4, Python 3.12.13 and official Triton-Ascend 3.6.0: a
    complete recursive run finished with **2,261 passed, 358 skipped, 0
    failed/errors**, exit code 0. The three previously failing FP32 cases
    passed in this full run.
    - A5 / Ascend950, Python 3.11.10 and official Triton-Ascend 3.2.2: a
    complete recursive run finished with **1,314 passed, 1,305 skipped, 0
    failed/errors**, exit code 0. Ordinary RoPE and vnorm entries are
    limited to A2/A3; their A5 cases are skipped.
    - Known compiler, hardware-contract and operator failures are explicitly
    scoped skips, not numerical passes or kernel fixes. BF16 sigmoid/exp
    compiler-incompatible cases remain skipped for A3; this PR does not
    change operator implementations.
    - The 13 updated test files still match the validated snapshot after
    merging main. Ruff lint/format, AST/source checks,
    package-init/context-manager checks and pytest/JUnit accounting passed.
    `bash format.sh ci` was attempted locally but did not complete while
    installing actionlint's Go environment; the full repository check
    remains for CI.
    
    #### Trigger nightly
    
    Users with `triage` or higher permission can post these as separate PR
    comments:
    
    ```text
    /nightly singlecard-ops-a3 --a3-560t
    ```
    
    ```text
    /nightly singlecard-ops-a5
    ```
    
    ---
    
    ### Checklist
    
    #### Testing
    
    - [x] **Boundary / edge-case coverage**: I reviewed whether this change
    involves
    boundary conditions (e.g. empty input, single/zero element, min/max
    values,
    off-by-one, sequence-length limits, integer overflow). Where applicable,
    I
    added unit tests covering these edge cases in `tests/ut/` or
    `tests/e2e/`.
    - [ ] **Regression test**: If this PR fixes a bug, I added a regression
    test
      that would fail without the fix.
    - [x] **Error / failure path coverage**: I covered abnormal paths
    (exceptions,
    timeouts, out-of-range, division by zero) in addition to the happy path.
    - [x] **Meaningful & reliable tests**: New tests assert real behavior
    and are
      not written merely to satisfy CI.
    - [ ] **Performance impact**: If this PR touches a performance-sensitive
    path,
      I attached benchmark results and added performance regression tests.
    
    Existing operator cases are reused, with focused quantization-reference
    and A5 backend regression coverage. No operator kernels or production
    runtime behavior are changed; skipped cases are reported separately and
    no performance improvement is claimed.
    
    
